{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A dismissal between review-page reads can cause the factory to merge without a current qualifying approval, but the scenario requires a multi-page review list and narrow timing."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A newer recorded change request can be ignored, allowing a merge based on stale approval evidence during a realistic polling race."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Queuing an external PR with the approval option unset causes extra polling and CI feed notifications."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The guide omits the final review-to-merge timing limitation and the stricter branch-protection option."}]}